  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby approved shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans with the approved plans which forms part of this notice. \r \rLocation Plan; Block Plan; Highway impact assessment; Flood Risk Assessment; 26_1097_100 Rev B;  26_1097_101 Rev B; 26_1097_102 Rev B; 26_1097_103 Rev B; 26_1097_104 Rev B; 26_1097_105 Rev B; 26_1097_106 Rev B.\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning. \r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the kitchen/dining room  and shall be retained as such, in accordance with the approved plans, in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the cycle parking spaces proposed have been fully constructed in accordance with the hereby approved details and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.  \r\rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport. \r",
    "Prior to occupation of the development hereby permitted, the refuse and recycling storage hereby approved shall be provided in accordance with the approved details and thereafter maintained unless otherwise submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets. \r\r",
    "The premises shall be occupied by no more than six persons as a House in Multiple Occupation falling within Use Class C4 and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained residential units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Prior to first occupation of the HMO use, and notwithstanding the submitted site plan, a revised site plan showing the car parking space, the location of proposed cycle parking to the front garden and refuse storage, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall be carried in accordance with the approved details prior to occupation of the development.\r \rReason: To ensure the site can accommodate appropriate car parking and compliant cycle and refuse storage for the development to accord with planning policy\r",
    "The outbuilding shown on the approved plans shall only be used for purposes incidental to the occupation of the House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved and shall not be occupied as sleeping accommodation, a self-contained residential unit or for any separate primary use at any time.\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for occupiers, safeguard neighbouring amenity and prevent the creation of an additional residential unit without planning permission.\r\r"
  ],
